  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"12.2.2\"\n\npackage:\n  name: pyobjc-framework-coreaudio\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/p/pyobjc-framework-CoreAudio/pyobjc_framework_coreaudio-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 880214f7328d6502a0c60ee744fa1eabe77a0d0c9ae276009453b69474eacf38\n\nbuild:\n  number: 2\n  skip: not osx\n  script:\n    content:\n      # force pyobjc to use conda-forge's chosen SDK\n      - export CFLAGS=\"${CFLAGS} -isysroot ${SDKROOT:-$CONDA_BUILD_SYSROOT}\"\n      - ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n  host:\n    - python\n    - pip\n    - setuptools\n    - wheel\n  run:\n    # upstream metadata only requires >=12.0; the <13 cap guards against\n    # mixing pyobjc major versions, which are released and ABI-matched in\n    # lockstep\n    - python\n    - pyobjc-core >=${{ version }},<13\n    - pyobjc-framework-cocoa >=${{ version }},<13\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - CoreAudio\n      pip_check: true\n\nabout:\n  summary: Wrappers for the framework CoreAudio on macOS\n  description: |\n    PyObjC wrappers for Apple's CoreAudio framework, giving Python access\n    to the macOS audio hardware abstraction layer (audio devices, streams,\n    and their properties). Part of the PyObjC project, which provides\n    bridges between Python and Objective-C frameworks on macOS.\n  license: MIT\n  license_file: License.txt\n  homepage: https://pyobjc.readthedocs.io/\n  repository: https://github.com/ronaldoussoren/pyobjc\n  documentation: https://pyobjc.readthedocs.io/\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - ruben-arts\n",
